/Title (Hedge funds have access to strategic tools that traditional managers often cannot use as flexibly, including long and short positions, tactical hedging, derivatives, and dynamic portfolio adjustments. Managers also frequently invest their own capital alongside clients, creating stronger alignment of interests. This combination of flexibility, active risk management, and aligned incentives allows hedge funds to pursue absolute returns across different market conditions, seeking opportunities in both rising and falling markets while managing downside risk.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2602 0 R
